---
layout: base.njk
section: home
---
<div class="hero">
  <div class="plate">
    <div class="photo"><img src="{{ '/img/me.jpg' | url }}" alt="Oliver Ye" width="200" height="250"></div>
    <p class="photo-caption">smoothie not worth it</p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p class="lede">Hi! I'm Oliver. I'm fascinated by how computers work, I enjoy reading American history, and I daydream about building gizmos and gadgets.</p>
    <p>I've always found writing to be a useful tool for putting structure on free-floating ideas, and my motivation for this blog was to create a place for those thoughts to settle.</p>
    <p>Underneath all of this is a belief that it's important to remain a life-long learner across all disciplines and to do so with a certain amount of rigor. We live in a complex, ever-changing reality and I find that each field offers a framework for understanding the mechanics by which institutions and other people affect us. The decisions we make will still be human ones, with murky notions of right and wrong, but I gain more conviction knowing they were made with some clarity about how the world works, rather than carelessness.</p>
    <div class="rail mono">
      <a href="{{ site.links.github }}">github</a>
      <a href="{{ site.links.email }}">email</a>
      <a href="{{ site.links.linkedin }}">linkedin</a>
      <a href="{{ '/feed.xml' | url }}">rss</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="recent">
  <h2>Recent</h2>
  <ul>
    {%- for post in collections.everything | take(5) %}
    <li>
      <span class="when">{{ post.date | date }}</span>
      <span>
        <a href="{{ post.data.link or (post.url | url) }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a>
        <span class="where">— {{ post.data.section | sectionTitle }}</span>
      </span>
    </li>
    {%- else %}
    <li><span class="where">Nothing posted yet.</span></li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
